---
/**
 * Security meta tags shared by every page (issue #144, F-SEC-003).
 *
 * The site deploys to GitHub Pages, which cannot emit custom HTTP headers,
 * so the enforceable subset lands here as document-level meta:
 *
 *  - `<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy">` — a meta-delivered CSP.
 *    Scoped to what the build actually emits: 'unsafe-inline' on script-src
 *    and style-src is *required* (the is:inline consent gate, inlined module
 *    scripts, onclick handlers, and <style is:global> blocks would all be
 *    blocked without it); the only third-party origin is the path-scoped
 *    googletagmanager /gtag/ loader that ConsentManager injects after an
 *    explicit Accept, and GA4's own collect endpoints on connect-src.
 *    `frame-ancestors` is intentionally absent — the CSP spec ignores it in
 *    meta delivery; it lives in `public/_headers` for hosts that honor HTTP
 *    headers. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md for the full model.
 *  - `<meta name="referrer">` — the referrer policy browsers honor today.
 *
 * Clickjacking protection (frame-ancestors / X-Frame-Options) is not
 * expressible via meta on GitHub Pages; `public/_headers` carries it for
 * Netlify/Cloudflare Pages deployments.
 */
---

<meta
  http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"
  content="default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests"
/>
<meta name="referrer" content="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" />
